From: Jocelyn Berrendonner <jocelynb@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] kvm: skip generic kvm_arch_has_private_mem when arch defines it

The arm64 Microsoft Azure Linux (CBL-Mariner) kernel tree defines
kvm_arch_has_private_mem() as a macro in arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h.
The generic definition in include/linux/kvm_host.h is a static inline guarded
only by !CONFIG_KVM_GENERIC_MEMORY_ATTRIBUTES. On a Kata GPU UVM the guest
kernel is built without KVM, so CONFIG_KVM_GENERIC_MEMORY_ATTRIBUTES is unset
and the generic inline is emitted even though the arch macro already exists.
The macro then expands into the inline's signature and
arch/arm64/kernel/asm-offsets.c fails to compile:

  include/linux/kvm_host.h: error: expected identifier or '(' before 'struct'
  arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h: in definition of macro
  'kvm_arch_has_private_mem'

Also skip the generic inline when the arch already provides the macro,
mirroring the upstream '#ifndef kvm_arch_has_private_mem' idiom.

Signed-off-by: Jocelyn Berrendonner <jocelynb@microsoft.com>
Generated-By: GitHub Copilot
---
 include/linux/kvm_host.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/kvm_host.h b/include/linux/kvm_host.h
--- a/include/linux/kvm_host.h
+++ b/include/linux/kvm_host.h
@@ -721,8 +721,8 @@ static inline int kvm_arch_vcpu_memslots_id(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
 	return 0;
 }
 #endif
 
-#ifndef CONFIG_KVM_GENERIC_MEMORY_ATTRIBUTES
+#if !defined(CONFIG_KVM_GENERIC_MEMORY_ATTRIBUTES) && !defined(kvm_arch_has_private_mem)
 static inline bool kvm_arch_has_private_mem(struct kvm *kvm)
 {
 	return false;
